From cee9c454eae4789ad90cee7e1955a1fd3e04e41f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: halt95 <halt95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 02:49:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 96/97] scheduler: release a waiter's pin on the deferred free
 path too

The scheduler takes pop_blocks_for_free when a step may still be in
flight, for example when a preempted request is aborted before its
fence drained. A waiting request's pin is never written by any step, so
it is now released there at once. Before, it stayed until the next
yield or reset, keeping its blocks pinned and a waiter slot taken.

pin_waiting_hit touches each block in the pool it belongs to; private
pool groups route like free_blocks. Its docstring states the known gap:
a pin is a snapshot of the hit at pin time. It is not refreshed if the
hit grows while the request waits, or if a producer moves a pinned live
block's hash into its copy. The admission lookup still sees whatever is
cached, so the cost is a smaller hit, never a wrong one.
MAX_PINNED_WAITERS goes from 8 to 16.

Test: a pinned waiter popped through the deferred path leaves no pin,
no waiter slot and the pool at its baseline.
---
